A||||2||Fformula88||How do I find out what year engine is in my Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||Fformula88||03-17-2000||09:55 PM||||I have a 1988 Fiero Formula, but have had lots of problems with it running.  I am suspicious that its V6 is out of a different year Fiero, which could be the cause of my problems.  I also cannot seem to find or see the block serial number on the backside of the engine.  Is there any other obviuous differences that could set the 88 V6 apart from a previous year?  Maybe a different part?  I also know of the different intake plenums, and mine DOES NOT have the engraved Fiero, but has the sticker.  I believe all 88's have it engraved.  Thanx for any help or advice you can give.<P>John||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||03-18-2000||01:15 AM||||1985 2.8 CBX, CBY<BR>1986 2.8 DAF, DAH, DBN<BR>1987 2.8 SCN, SCP<BR>1988 2.8 CFC, CFD<BR>Engine number location: front of block below right cylinder head.<P>85 and 86 V-6 has the sticker manifold.<BR>87 and 88 V-6 has the engraved manifold.<BR>Hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||03-18-2000||02:41 AM||||Thanx Oreif!  I'll take a look tomorrow.  I know it has a sticker on the intake manifold, but also has the exhaust manifold for an 88!  Thanx for those codes!||||reg||1
